# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITAL Web — client environment
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables belong here. Everything in this file is compiled
# into the browser bundle and is publicly readable.
#
# NEVER copy values from apps/api/.env into this file. The web client must not
# hold the Supabase service key, the database URL, the Paymob secrets, or the
# Anthropic key — it talks to the VITAL API, and the API holds those.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the VITAL API, including the /api/v1 prefix.
# Local development (the API listens on 3000; this web app runs on 3003):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1

# Production (set this in the Vercel project, then REDEPLOY — NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values are inlined at build time, so adding the variable alone changes
# nothing until the next build):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://vital-t0y2.onrender.com/api/v1
#
# A production build with this unset no longer falls back to localhost: every
# request fails immediately with an explicit "API address is missing" error
# instead of a mystery network failure. See lib/api.ts.
